    "q-161587": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161587",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14245698/assets/5151df3c5b84ffaca9aa16b401cd9364fea10a240d39c9c28d815b36e417b16d.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=1-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=1-x\\,\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-161587-a",
