    "q-161440": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161440",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14245698/assets/b0c3e30fcb7e748a80cdf98892291599967151343efe671aca790b2528039c4c.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4\\,\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
