    "q-64991": {
      "dom_id": "step-q64991",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x<0,\\,0\\le y<2\\}\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}},\\,0<y<2\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14245698/assets/71851a12f638da9604450cae0d50ed15187e850368890845d60b16b89e728bcf.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14245698/assets/abdd434da59bb3a1bdc0ee7de398d7ea4aeae2f617f54b5a26a5bad871ba0ac4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<2\\,\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
